The attached image, corresponding to Figure 2A and 2B in the PDF, provides physical characterization of the Nano-11 nanoparticles, which are investigated as vaccine adjuvants. Figure 2A is a transmission electron micrograph (TEM) showing Nano-11 as spherical particles with an irregular, cauliflower-like appearance, with a scale bar of 50 nm. Figure 2B presents the diameter distribution of Nano-11 as determined by dynamic light scattering (DLS), indicating a relatively uniform size range, with the Z-average hydrodynamic diameter consistently between 75 and 80 nm.